# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#161), L §8.2 One read set (R7): an entry is listed exactly when a read in its set gives it, so an
# ask's with pin that no read of the line takes isn't listed: a reads d, which never reads flag, and lists nothing; b
# reads e, which takes the pin (10.00 PLN), and lists it; c lists it once for its two values. 2.1.7's refcore (and the
# M2 engine) listed every written pin.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input x: money PLN
input flag: int

def d: money PLN
  rule base = x + x

def e: money PLN
  rule base = x * flag

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = 10.00 PLN "s"
  flag = 2 "s"

ask a: d with flag = 1
ask b: e with flag = 1
ask c: d, e with flag = 3
=== expect
a: 20.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
b: 10.00 PLN
  pinned: flag = 1
  cut 2026-03-01
c: (20.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN)
  pinned: flag = 3
  cut 2026-03-01
